# markdown-syntax AST->HTML conformance suite v1: syntax decisions
source: gfm_extensions
decision: Tables, task list items, and inline footnotes are part of the syntax.
count: 3

--- case 1 options allow_dangerous_html,allow_dangerous_protocol label-bytes 66 input-bytes 17 expected-bytes 94
from commonmark/gfm_table.cases #1; verified: cmark-gfm, micromark
--- input
| a |
| - |
| b |
--- expected
<table>
<thead>
<tr>
<th>a</th>
</tr>
</thead>
<tbody>
<tr>
<td>b</td>
</tr>
</tbody>
</table>
--- end
--- case 2 options allow_dangerous_html,allow_dangerous_protocol label-bytes 75 input-bytes 8 expected-bytes 71
from commonmark/gfm_task_list_item.cases #1; verified: cmark-gfm, micromark
--- input
* [x] y.
--- expected
<ul>
<li><input type="checkbox" disabled="" checked="" /> y.</li>
</ul>
--- end
--- case 3 options allow_dangerous_html,allow_dangerous_protocol label-bytes 91 input-bytes 30 expected-bytes 384
from gfm/inline_footnotes.cases #10; decision 0007: inline footnotes are part of the syntax
--- input
Text^[note] should not parse.

--- expected
<p>Text<sup class="footnote-ref"><a href="#fn-__inline_1" id="fnref-__inline_1" data-footnote-ref>1</a></sup> should not parse.</p>
<section class="footnotes" data-footnotes>
<ol>
<li id="fn-__inline_1">
<p>note <a href="#fnref-__inline_1" class="footnote-backref" data-footnote-backref data-footnote-backref-idx="1" aria-label="Back to reference 1">↩</a></p>
</li>
</ol>
</section>
--- end
